## MIAO-GTNH

betterquesting.questline.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=MIAO-GTNH
betterquesting.questline.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=The combined MIAO-GTNH questline (110 quests, two directions). Direction one — the era spine: a root quest and seven era gates spread along the X axis from Steam to LuV with zero cross-gate edges, so you may enter at any era; gate wings and pain-point quests hand you tools at each era's key bottlenecks. Direction two — the three-mod integration district: GTSR's steam-economy hub, GTSWN's wireless grid, and GTIT's neko economy and rings — three subtrees, none era-gated. Plus a LuV+ open line (bee genetics and endgame manifestos) and the graduation quest "The Master" — also the key to the vending machine's Endgame Exchange page (gate 5569054221778550784:110).%n%nBlueprint: plan/blueprint/bq-miao.md v1; built by plan/build/build_bq_miao.py.
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§3§lMIAO-GTNH!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=Welcome to §3§lMIAO-GTNH§r — where three tech lines converge: §6GTSR§r makes steam great again, §3GTSWN§r cuts every last cable, and §dGTIT§r turns the economy into a game.%n%nThis book does not replace the GTNH questline. It does two things only: hands you a tool at §1every era's§r key pain point, and weaves the three mods into your progression.%n%n§cWarning: this pack never gates an era. Skip steam and rush HV — the tool quests will wait. §r%n%n§8§oUnboxing bonus: take the cat's welcome kit, then start with the quest at your feet. HAJIMI HAJIMI.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.name=§1§lHammer Blows!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.desc=Starting from nothing — not even an axe for the trees? GTNH's day one begins with wood, and with blistered knuckles.%n%nHand over §1 16 logs§r — that plain. The questbook pays an §1iron pickaxe, axe and shovel§r; leave the hammering to tools.%n%n§cWarning: the logs are consumed — keep a margin for expansion. §r%n%n§8§oEvery great assembly line's first day smells of sawdust.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.name=§2§lFood Is Heaven!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.desc=Hunger is heaven's own law, and bread is the engineer's fuel. In early GTNH a bowl of stew counts as a feast — the food bar bottoms out before any voltage does.%n%nHand in §1 16 wheat§r for §1 16 bread§r and a cake — agriculture is industry's first workshop.%n%n§cWarning: the wheat is consumed, but the field grows back. §r%n%n§8§oThe cake is no lie here; it is the opening snack.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.name=§3§lWater Without End!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.desc=Hauling water bucket by bucket? Early chemistry sends you to the well three times per condenser; the buckets wear out before the blueprints do.%n%nTrade §1 16 water buckets§r for §1two cauldrons§r and survive the condenser age. The true endless water waits at the §dGTIT hub§r — the infinity fluid cell, one item, one ocean.%n%n§cWarning: the buckets are consumed — do not mourn the iron. §r%n%n§8§oBefore you own the ocean, learn to carry a bucket.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.name=§6§lBegone, Evil!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.desc=The mooing in the dark is not romance, it is a loss report. GTNH nights run colder than vanilla — lighting is the defense of your throughput.%n%nHand in §1 32 torches§r to light the radius, earn §1 16 glowstone dust§r — the down payment on next tunnel's lamps.%n%n§cWarning: the torches are consumed; place enough first. §r%n%n§8§oLight is order; only creepers live in the shadows.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.name=§2§lHunger, Begone!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.desc=Steak feeds the moment; golden carrots feed the marathon. When the line runs past two in the morning, the hunger bar shows no mercy.%n%nTrade §1 16 cooked beef§r for §1 8 golden carrots§r — a rehearsal for the all-nighter ration.%n%n§cWarning: the beef is consumed — save two for supper. §r%n%n§8§oGolden carrot: the only legal performance enhancer.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.name=§1§lHuge! Huge! Huge Capacity!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.desc=Thirty-six slots in the pack, thirty-six hundred in the dream. GTNH's intermediates fall thicker than snow, and the chest is first-generation storage.%n%nHand in §1 8 leather§r and §1 8 string§r for §1 8 chests§r — the first brick of a storage wall.%n%n§cWarning: the materials are consumed — count your stock first. §r%n%n§8§oOne day you will own quantum storage; tonight, lean on the wall.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.name=§8§lNo Sky Island?
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.desc=Not every save spawns with a sky island. Platforms, treehouses, floating factories? Territorial expansion starts with saplings.%n%nHand in §1 16 saplings§r for §1 4 slime balls§r and §1 8 vines§r — seed capital for vertical architecture.%n%n§cWarning: the saplings are consumed. Keep a few — sustainability matters. §r%n%n§8§oSlime ball: the penny stock of vertical transit.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.name=§4§lHigher Grade!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.desc=Obsidian is patience made solid. Reaching it means you have crossed the watershed between stone and iron.%n%nShow §1 16 obsidian§r — display-only, a glance and done — and the questbook pays §1 4 diamonds§r as the down payment on a diamond pickaxe.%n%n§cWarning: nothing is taken, but it must truly be in your pack. §r%n%n§8§oAfter the diamond pickaxe there are no unbreakable blocks — only unwanted ones.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.name=§2§lFinding Your Feet
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.desc=Tools, food, storage — you have walked all three roads a little. Now show one family asset: §1 16 chests§r, §1 32 iron ingots§r or §1 16 gold ingots§r, any one of the three.%n%nThe starter belt graduates here. The reward is §1 2 neko coins§r plus a pick-your-own bundle; the era gates wait to the east.%n%n§cWarning: pick one of three, display-only — but pick what you truly have. §r%n%n§8§oFamily assets are ranked not by price but by order of arrival.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.name=§6§lSteam! Steam! Steam!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.desc=Hands cramping from shoveling coal? GTNH's own steam tier has taught you the meaning of §1manpower boilers§r.%n%nHere is MIAO's steam graduation: show §1 8 steam casings§r, §1 4 sets of steam circuits§r and an §1 LV machine hull§r, and bid the coal age farewell.%n%n§cWarning: this gate never asks for GTSR machines — mods are tools, not tickets. §rAfterwards you may hand your steam to GTSR, but that is your choice, not the questbook's.%n%n§8§oSteam supplies are stocked in the vending machine's "Hardware Pack" page — completing this quest unlocks it.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.name=§6§lThe First Bronze
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.desc=Brass gets the fame, but bronze founded the GTNH republic. Your first bronze furnace deserves a paired debut.%n%nShow §1 2§r bronze furnaces — the hearths of the steam age. The questbook pays §1 32 coal§r for kindling.%n%n§cWarning: display-only — the machines stay with you and keep working. §r%n%n§8§oThe bronze furnace: a workhorse firing from prehistory to the late game.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.name=§6§lSun on the Roof!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.desc=Coal must be mined and trees planted; only sunlight is free. Putting the sun on the roof is the steam age's most dignified saving.%n%nShow §1 4§r steam solar units — the front row of the rooftop array. Earn §1 32 glass§r for the next greenhouse.%n%n§cWarning: solar eats weather, not fuel — keep a boiler on night shift. §r%n%n§8§oSunlight burns no coal, but it burns capital — the upfront cost stings.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.name=§6§lHigher! Hotter! More Steam!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.desc=Low-pressure boilers simmer; high-pressure boilers roar. Doubling output was never about burning more — it is about burning harder.%n%nShow §1 2§r high-pressure boilers, earn §1 16 sets of steam circuits§r — the work order for a pressure upgrade.%n%n§cWarning: higher pressure doubles the blast radius; do not skimp on blast walls. §r%n%n§8§oFirst rule of boiler discipline: never stand on its bad side.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.name=§1§lBoiler Discipline
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.desc=An unexploded boiler is the engineer's bare minimum. Fuel discipline starts with bookkeeping: so much coal in, so much steam out.%n%nHand in §1 32 coal§r for §1 8 coal blocks§r — compressed storage, banked futures.%n%n§cWarning: the coal is consumed. Boiler repairs cost far more than this heap ever will. §r%n%n§8§oAccounting is a prerequisite of boiler engineering.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.name=§3§lThe Steam Backbone
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.desc=Late steam era, a long steam-hauling road runs between boiler room and workshop. Pipes grow longer, pressure math grows tiresome.%n%n§6GTSR§r's steam hub array annexes your steam network for you: one backbone through, every branch served. Show §1 1§r unit.%n%n§cWarning: this quest's prerequisite is a soft link — no era gate involved. Mods are tools, not tickets. §r%n%n§8§oRaise the hub first; catch up on steam class later.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.name=§1§lCharcoal Economy
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.desc=Coal seams run out; forests do not. Charcoaling is the oldest fuel futures market: an axe today, a carbon warehouse tomorrow.%n%nHand in §1 32 charcoal§r for §1 32 coal§r — an equivalent exchange between two fuels at a fixed rate.%n%n§cWarning: the charcoal is consumed; keep the kilns on schedule. §r%n%n§8§oIt is not only the trees that are renewable — so is the peace of mind.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.name=§2§lWhite-Glove Delivery
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.desc=To enter the GTSR hub, hand in a calling card first. The Hub Singularity Chip is that white glove — the look-but-keep kind.%n%nShow §1 1§r chip to prove you have knocked on the steam economy's door. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Refills come later via the vending machine's "Singularity Exchange" page — see "One-Ticket Direct". §r%n%n§8§oWhite-glove rule: touching counts.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.name=§3§lCurrent Lights the World
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.desc=The first current across your skin feels like a tingle. GTNH's LV hands out no free electricity — it collects homework.%n%nShow §1 8 sets of LV circuits§r and §1 2 LV machine hulls§r, and the low-voltage club issues your card on the spot. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r, §1 2 neko coins§r, plus §1 8 sets of LV circuits§r back.%n%n§cWarning: this gate tests GT-native items only. Skip everything before — come straight to the gate of your own era. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the vending machine's "LV Circuit Pack" wholesale page.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.name=§3§lThe Way of Sensors
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.desc=Automation is not magic — it is perception. Machines cannot speak; sensors speak for them.%n%nShow §1 4§r sensors — the first synapses of your workshop's nervous system. Earn §1 32 redstone§r for the wiring ahead.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Redstone runs dry eventually; do not ration sensors as if they were redstone. §r%n%n§8§oOnly those who hear the machines' heartbeat may make them work overtime.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.name=§3§lFirst Wireless Sip
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.desc=The moment LV power arrives, you learn what cabling hell means — a wall of wire just to deliver a few dozen LU.%n%n§3GTSWN§r's wireless energy tap pulls the wires for you: §1 1§r unit, plug and draw. Craft it — this quest binds to no era gate.%n%n§cWarning: wireless is not limitless — the EU at the source is still yours to generate. §r%n%n§8§oEvery cable cut tastes of freedom.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.name=§3§lTwo-Way Street
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.desc=Power only flows in? Back-feeding remote generators is the other half of a wireless network's homework.%n%nCraft §1 2§r wireless dynamo covers — draw in, push out, both directions at once; islanded turbines join the grid from here.%n%n§cWarning: the covers do not manage existing loads; arrange your own overload protection. §r%n%n§8§oEU coming, EU going — that is a two-way street.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.name=§6§lThe Steam-to-Power Bridge
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.desc=The most awkward asset of the LV era is surplus steam — boilers still burning while the machines went electric.%n%n§6GTSR§r's large steam-to-power multiblock is that bridge: steam in, electricity out. Show §1 1§r — soft-linked prerequisite, no gate.%n%n§cWarning: conversion efficiency devalues era by era; do not stake your whole fortune on turbines. §r%n%n§8§oSteam: from leading role to supplier.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.name=§c§lThe Redstone Bank
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.desc=Redstone is Minecraft's hard currency and automation's monetary base. The bigger the deposit, the thicker the wire.%n%nDeposit §1 128 redstone§r, withdraw §1 16 glowstone dust§r — redstone interest converted into light.%n%n§cWarning: the redstone is consumed. Do not empty the vault — automation's foundation must not go bare. §r%n%n§8§oThe Redstone Bank never fails; it merely gets emptied by you.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.name=§6§lBronze's Swan Song
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.desc=Bronze has kept you company since day one. Before the substation rises, hold a farewell review for the old veterans.%n%nShow §1 16§r bronze furnaces on parade — the steam honor guard at full strength. Reward: §1 64 coal§r, the last batch of fuel they will ever burn.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. They can fight on for three more eras. §r%n%n§8§oA swan song is not a discharge — it is a transfer to the reserves.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.name=§5§lMedium Voltage, Heavy Alloys
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.desc=MV's ticket of entry is heavy alloys: §1 4 sets of MV circuits§r, §1 1 MV machine hull§r, §1 16 aluminium plates§r. Voltage doubles; so do the materials.%n%nReward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r, §1 2 neko coins§r, §1 16 aluminium plates§r back.%n%n§cWarning: the gate honors GT-native items only. Skip the earlier eras if you like — starting from MV works too. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the "Plate Wholesale" alumina/gem-dust page.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.name=§5§l"Rare" Metals!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.desc=Some metals are called rare yet flow steadier than copper; some lie everywhere and only show their worth when you need them.%n%nShow §1 16§r "rare" metal ingots — display-only. Reward: §1 8§r of the same back. Rare or not, the market decides.%n%n§cWarning: nothing is taken, but it must truly be in your pack. §r%n%n§8§o"Rare" is a marketing word; stock is a physical quantity.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.name=§1§lEmergency Alumina!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.desc=The week the aluminium runs dry, the whole MV line loses sleep together. Alumina is aluminium's blood — and anxiety's wellspring.%n%nShow §1 512§r alumina in stock — the decent floor of an emergency reserve. Reward: §1 64§r finished plates to plug the gap.%n%n§cWarning: display-only, but stock it for real — supply cuts never call ahead. §r%n%n§8§oInventory is the specific remedy for insomnia.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.name=§3§lThe Alumina Works
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.desc=From emergency hoard to standing factory — that is the MV engineer's coming of age. After this step, shortage anxiety becomes capacity planning.%n%nShow §1 128§r alumina output — the acceptance sheet of factory-scale throughput. Reward: §1 64 iron ingots§r, so the infrastructure never rusts.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Leave headroom for maintenance when planning capacity. §r%n%n§8§oA factory's mark is not its machine count but its sound sleep.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.name=§5§lThe Clay Miracle
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.desc=In GTNH the lowliest clay transforms into the skeleton of chemistry. Mud from the riverbed holds up the sky of the medium-voltage era.%n%nHand in §1 128§r clay balls for §1 32§r alumina — the first exchange of mud into miracle.%n%n§cWarning: the clay is consumed. Bring air before you dredge the riverbed. §r%n%n§8§oNever underestimate any lump of mud — it may be wearing chemistry's crown.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.name=§3§lThe Super Brain
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.desc=The MV workshop grows a central nervous system — a multiblock controller, and recipes stop traveling by hand.%n%nShow §1 1§r era-class multiblock controller. A GT native, bound to no mod.%n%n§cWarning: the brain makes no decisions for you; it only saves you the walk back. §r%n%n§8§oFrom here the workshop has a nervous system — and you are the commander.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.name=§d§lThe Mind's Eye
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.desc=Two hours prospecting, five minutes mining — GTNH's surveying routine turns every map into pencil scratch.%n%n§dGTIT§r's telekinesis ore scanner core: §1 19×19 chunks§r swept in one pass. Craft §1 1§r and bid blind-man's-bluff farewell.%n%n§cWarning: scanning eats power and patience alike; vein distribution rules are still yours to memorize. §r%n%n§8§oTelekinesis: outsourcing the legwork to technology.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.name=§4§lHigh Voltage, New Rules
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.desc=HV is not a bigger number — it is new rules: §1 4 sets of HV circuits§r, §1 1 HV machine hull§r, §1 16 titanium plates§r.%n%nFusion is still far off, but titanium is already knocking. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r, §1 2 neko coins§r, §1 16 titanium plates§r back.%n%n§cWarning: the gate tests GT-native items — starting your story at HV is fine too. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the "Plate Wholesale" titanium/tungstensteel page.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.name=§1§lThe Petrochemical Advice
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.desc=The moment HV arrives, petrochemistry's seed should go into the ground. Oil waits for no one — nor do pipelines and tanks.%n%nShow §1 16 sets§r of HV circuits — the ticket to the petrochemical line. Reward: §1 8 sets§r back, enough to break ground.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Petrochemistry is a marathon; do not sprint the start. §r%n%n§8§oOil is ancient sunlight — do not waste it flaring in place.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.name=§4§lThe Big One
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.desc=The HV workshop welcomes its first giant — an era-class large multiblock. Reinforce the foundation first, and your nerve along with it.%n%nShow §1 1§r large era-class machine. GT native — versatile and imposing.%n%n§cWarning: the big one eats structure and power alike; undervolt it and it strikes. §r%n%n§8§oThe day it moved in, every machine in the shop went quiet for three seconds.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.name=§1§lThe Fuel Advice
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.desc=The lesson on energy density is taught at HV. Loose coal cannot feed big machines; compressed fuel is the proper meal.%n%nHand in §1 32§r coal blocks for §1 8 sets§r of HV circuits — the equivalent of a fuel upgrade.%n%n§cWarning: the blocks are consumed. Keep the boiler room or the oil field on overtime — at least one. §r%n%n§8§oYour fuel's tier decides your machines' appetite.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.name=§4§lBedrock of Bricks
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.desc=Big machines stand firm only on a thick floor. Stone brick is industrial aesthetics — and load-bearing structure.%n%nShow §1 256§r stone — display-only. Reward: §1 64 iron ingots§r, the skeleton of a reinforced floor.%n%n§cWarning: the stone stays with you. The floor's thickness decides the ceiling's weight. §r%n%n§8§oGreat machines stand on unglamorous stone.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.name=§1§lTitanium Solo
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.desc=Titanium is HV's main melody: light, hard, expensive. One titanium line, half a history of HV.%n%nShow §1 64§r titanium plates — the solo enters its cadenza. Reward: §1 32 gold ingots§r, the conductor's salary.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Titanium's supply chain is long and brittle; arrange the accompaniment before the solo. §r%n%n§8§oTitanium does not sing — titanium only goes hardcore.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJw.name=§3§lWatching the Watts
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJw.desc=The anxieties of an HV grid: where did the power go? Why another trip? What you lack is not more energy — it is sight.%n%n§3GTSWN§r's energy monitor (§1 1§r unit) hangs on the grid, and every watt gets a ledger entry.%n%n§cWarning: monitoring generates nothing — but invisible problems are the most expensive ones. §r%n%n§8§oData will not save the grid, but it will save your sleep.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKA.name=§2§lExtreme Voltage, Big Stuff
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKA.desc=EV stands for Extreme Voltage and extreme billing: §1 4 sets of EV circuits§r, §1 1 EV machine hull§r, §1 16 tungstensteel plates§r.%n%nReward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r, §1 2 neko coins§r, §1 16 tungstensteel plates§r back — half the big fellow's grocery list paid upfront.%n%n§cWarning: the gate tests GT-native items — players starting from EV are just as welcome. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the "Nether Star Plate" page — restocked every 22 hours.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKQ.name=§2§lHeart of the Workstation
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKQ.desc=The nether star: the Wither's legacy and the workstation's pacemaker. Without it, EV-grade precision manufacturing is a non-starter.%n%nShow §1 2§r nether stars — display-only; the Wither is dead, burn paper offerings if you must. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r.%n%n§cWarning: the Wither is easy; re-laying soul sand every time is the hard part. §r%n%n§8§oStars in the pack, heartbeat in the workshop.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKg.name=§1§lThe Vein Census
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKg.desc=An EV-scale mining plan begins with a serious vein census. Data does not lie, and the pickaxe stops swinging in vain — the more diligent the survey, the fewer wasted trips.%n%nHand in §1 64 iron ore§r and §1 32 diamond ore§r — raw census samples, collected for the archive.%n%n§cWarning: the samples are consumed. Smelt first if you want the metal kept. §r%n%n§8§oThe end of geology is logistics.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.name=§6§lFirst Sign of a Singularity
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.desc=By EV the steam economy has outgrown ordinary ledgers. The singularity is steam's crystallized form — and its surplus grain.%n%nShow §1 8§r Steam Entangled Singularities — GTSR hard currency's first bundled debut. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r.%n%n§cWarning: display-only, but do hoard them — the later "Singularity Chain" and endgame exchanges are all priced in these. §r%n%n§8§oBurn steam long enough and you burn out a black hole.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAALA.name=§1§lThe Energy Cliff
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAALA.desc=The EV consumption curve is a cliff: across it lies mass production; below it, a dead line.%n%nHand in §1 256§r glowstone dust — the lighting budget for the energy stairs — for §1 32 sets§r of EV circuits, turning the cliff into a ramp.%n%n§cWarning: the dust is consumed. Even the Nether's glowstone is a finite resource. §r%n%n§8§oThe cliff is not scary; setting out without rope is.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAALQ.name=§6§lThe Steam Mining Rig
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAALQ.desc=Still mining by hand in the EV era? Your steam empire should learn to go down the shaft on its own.%n%n§6GTSR§r's crust steam boring machine (§1 1§r unit): powered means mining, ore rides the steam. Soft-linked prerequisite, no gate.%n%n§cWarning: boring devours power — check the meter before you grid it. §r%n%n§8§oMaking steam bend over for you: the whole point of civilization.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAALg.name=§1§lThe Tungstensteel Flood
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAALg.desc=From 16 plates to 64 — forming a flood takes exactly one EV.%n%nShow §1 64§r tungstensteel plates — display-only. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r, the flood's admission ticket.%n%n§cWarning: the 64 must truly be in the pack — render distance is not a cheat code. §r%n%n§8§oThe flood asks not whence, but how much.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAALw.name=§d§lCapacity Without End!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAALw.desc=Past EV your storage is undergoing §ccosmic inflation§r: cells lined up row after row, while fluids still lean on buckets of §1fluid cells§r.%n%n§dGTIT§r's answer is brutal and elegant — the Infinity Fluid Cell. One fluid, one cell, §1Integer.MAX_VALUE§r bytes. The drivers will never seat fluids again.%n%n§cWarning: idle draw is §11 AE/t§r each — the more you plug in, the more it costs — but compared to your sanity, that is pocket change. §r%n%n§8§oAfter this quest, the infinity cell pair enters the "Endgame Exchange" page at 48 shimmering coins each.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMA.name=§1§lInsane Voltage
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMA.desc=Insane voltage, insane acceptance: §1 1 set of IV circuits§r, §1 1 IV machine hull§r, §1 4 IV-grade alloy plates§r. Few in number, startling in purity.%n%nReward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r, §1 2 neko coins§r, §1 8§r of the same alloy back.%n%n§cWarning: the gate tests GT-native items. Lunatics starting at IV are equally welcome. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the "Singularity Exchange" entry tier — 8 shimmering coins a lot, restocked every 22 hours.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQ.name=§6§lOverpressure License
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQ.desc=Ordinary hub chips hit their pressure ceiling the moment IV begins. The reinforced edition is the overpressure club's license — and proof of standing.%n%nShow §1 1§r Reinforced Hub Singularity Chip — display-only. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The premium on reinforced parts is the insurance premium. §r%n%n§8§oHang the license on the wall and run overpressure with ease.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMg.name=§c§lEve of Criticality
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMg.desc=The critical singularity: one more step and you stand at the threshold of a chain reaction. Late-IV you works the final shift on criticality's eve.%n%nShow §1 1§r Critical Steam Entangled Singularity. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r — the night-shift allowance.%n%n§cWarning: criticals are for admiring from afar. Display-only — and best not fiddled with. §r%n%n§8§oOn the eve of criticality, every engineer is a sleepless artist.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMw.name=§d§lFrequent Flyer
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMw.desc=Once flight becomes an addiction, every landing feels like exile. The charged float core swaps those wings for electric ones.%n%nShow §1 1§r electric float core — §dGTIT§r's electric ticket. Prerequisite softly links to "Flight!" — no gate involved.%n%n§cWarning: electric flight eats power, not food; budget your grid surplus first. §r%n%n§8§oA frequent flyer's only luggage is the power bill.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAANA.name=§8§lStardust Gleaning
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAANA.desc=Ender pearls are the seashells of the star-sea; name tags are their names. IV's romance is binding far-off fragments into an album.%n%nShow §1 16§r ender pearls and §1 8§r name tags — the gleaner's collector card. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Do not throw pearls — the one teleporting would be you. §r%n%n§8§oThe point of gleaning is not the shells but the number of bends.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAANQ.name=§6§lHeart of Lava
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAANQ.desc=Lava is the planet's blood and the cheapest heat source of the late game. Bucket it, haul it, done in one breath.%n%nHand in §1 16§r lava buckets for §1 32§r obsidian — the ancient transposition of fighting fire with fire.%n%n§cWarning: the buckets are consumed. Do not sprint while hauling — spilled lava has no undo. §r%n%n§8§oLava's heart beats beneath someone else's basement.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAANg.name=§3§lThe Circuit Tower
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAANg.desc=Stack EV circuits to 64 sets and you have a tower. At its top lives IV's freedom.%n%nShow §1 64§r sets of EV circuits — the tower topped out. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r and §1 16 sets§r back.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Circuit throughput is armament; do not leave the tower unfinished. §r%n%n§8§oThe secret of climbing: one floor at a time, eyes off the top.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAANw.name=§d§lFlight!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAANw.desc=Slow travel, brutal vertical work — GTNH's terrain never humors the hurrier. Staircases are optional.%n%nCraft §1 1§r float core: flight for hunger, a fair trade. §dGTIT§r make, bound to no era gate.%n%n§cWarning: hunger is the fuel. Pack rations before takeoff. §r%n%n§8§oFrom now on, gravity is merely a suggestion.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOA.name=§d§lLuV: Lighting the Way
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOA.desc=The L in LuV is both Lucrative and Lunatic: §1 1 LuV machine hull§r, §1 8 LuV-grade crystals§r, §1 1 set of LuV circuit boards§r.%n%nReward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r, §1 2 neko coins§r, §1 8§r crystals back.%n%n§cWarning: the gate tests GT-native items. Start at LuV and the questbook takes it all in stride. §r%n%n§8§oAfter this quest, the "Endgame Exchange" page becomes visible as a preview — goods still locked, window shopping open.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOQ.name=§3§lThe Assembly-Line Age
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOQ.desc=LuV recipes begin demanding the assembly line — the age of industrial flow has arrived. Blueprints are no longer a one-table affair.%n%nShow §1 1§r era-class assembly machine — GT's native large-line core, versatile and silent.%n%n§cWarning: structure checks are stricter than they look; leave the workshop its headroom. §r%n%n§8§oBetween workshop and factory lies exactly one assembly line.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOg.name=§3§lThe Lithography Sea
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOg.desc=LuV circuit output depends on the depth of your lithography stock. 32 sets is one ladle of the sea.%n%nShow §1 32 sets§r of lithography material — display-only. Reward: §1 16 sets§r back; the sea deepens another inch.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Treat the lithography chain's waste, or the sea keeps the ledger. §r%n%n§8§oMoore's law, translated: a lithography machine that never stops.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOw.name=§2§lThe Glutton's Feast
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOw.desc=LuV-era hauling starves the eyes into seeing stars. The Ring of Gluttony stands ready: wear it and hunger becomes folklore.%n%nShow §1 1§r Ring of Gluttony and §1 64§r cooked beef — the potluck entrance fee. A §dGTIT§r piece, soft-linked.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The ring cures hunger, not appetite — pack the steak anyway. §r%n%n§8§oA true feast is never glancing at the hunger bar again.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPA.name=§d§lThe Dragon Pact
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPA.desc=Many slay the dragon; few keep the egg. The dragon egg is the pact's seal: it will not hatch, but it witnesses.%n%nShow §1 1§r dragon egg — display-only, the pact signs itself. Reward: §1 2 shimmering coins§r, the contract's deposit.%n%n§cWarning: the egg is display-only — and do not perch it up high; gravity holds no reverence for pacts. §r%n%n§8§oThe dragon pact has one clause: never slay a second one.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPQ.name=§1§lCrystal Solo
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPQ.desc=At 64 diamonds they stop being jewelry and become feedstock — the entry material of the crystal age.%n%nShow §1 64§r diamonds — display-only. Reward: §1 2 sets§r of LuV circuit boards, the solo's accompaniment.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Only after diamond freedom does the true scarcity begin. §r%n%n§8§oCarbon's final form is the transistor's nostalgia.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPg.name=§3§lThe LuV Circuit Flood
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPg.desc=From 8 crystals to 64, LuV's appetite finally shows its true face — it eats not power but supply chains.%n%nShow §1 64§r LuV-grade crystals — the flood-tier acceptance. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. When crystal output lags, fix the upstream before cursing the downstream. §r%n%n§8§oBefore the flood, even monocrystalline silicon queues.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPw.name=§2§lThe Master's Threshold
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPw.desc=Before the endgame, one last threshold stands on diamond blocks. Sixteen of them — no more, no less — the weight of ceremony.%n%nShow §1 16§r diamond blocks — display-only. Behind the Master's threshold lies the full endgame shelf.%n%n§cWarning: the threshold looks but does not take. The real toll waits at "The Master". §r%n%n§8§oA threshold's purpose: make everyone who enters bow once.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQA.name=§2§lBeekeepers, Assemble!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQA.desc=After LuV everyone needs a hobby. Beekeeping is GTNH's hidden ending line: genetics, pedigrees, and the bees' foul temper.%n%nShow §1 2§r drones of any species — lineage irrelevant, attendance counts. Reward: §1 32§r sugar, the apiary's opening candy.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Bees sting — full armor beats a fine pedigree. §r%n%n§8§oBeekeeping lesson one: you do not own bees; you are their landlord.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQQ.name=§d§lThe Dob Dynasty
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQQ.desc=The DOB bee: GT genetics' gateway species. Breed a pure drone, land both alleles on chromosome 0, and the dynasty is founded.%n%nShow §1 1§r pure-bred DOB drone. Reward: a same-bloodline pure princess, plus §1 8§r Steam Entangled Singularities.%n%n§cWarning: display-only — but the NBT must be homozygous; hybrids fail the genetics exam. §r%n%n§8§oA dynasty's first cornerstone is a length of pure genes.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQg.name=§d§lThe Salismundus Empire
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQg.desc=The Salis Mundus bee: named for the salt of the world, ceiling of the saline lineage. The chemistry branch gains bee-power from here.%n%nShow §1 1§r pure-bred Salis Mundus drone. Reward: a same-bloodline princess and §1 8§r singularities — salinity maxed.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. In the saline pedigree race, the loser is always patience. §r%n%n§8§oSalt is first of all flavors and mother of the sodium chain.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQw.name=§d§lThe Shadowmetal Swarm
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQw.desc=The Shadowmetal bee: dark aristocracy whose production runs in the shadows. Breeding it is biological insurance for your rare metals.%n%nShow §1 1§r pure-bred Shadowmetal drone. Reward: a same-bloodline princess and §1 8§r singularities.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The shadow lineage's odds live up to the word "shadow". §r%n%n§8§oBees fly in the shade; ores stack in the sun.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAARA.name=§d§lThe Divided Hive
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAARA.desc=The Divided bee: one hive, two production lines. GT genetics' art of division — the antidote to resource anxiety.%n%nShow §1 1§r pure-bred Divided drone. Reward: a same-bloodline princess and §1 8§r singularities.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Its temper divides as well — schedule around its mood, not yours. §r%n%n§8§oSplitting in two is philosophy; splitting into many is throughput.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAARQ.name=§2§lThe Apiary Megaproject
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAARQ.desc=Four dynasties' princesses in one frame — the apiary megaproject tops out. Not a collection but the confluence of four gene rivers.%n%nShow §1 4§r pure princesses: Dob, Salis Mundus, Shadowmetal, Divided — one bloodline each, none optional.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Princesses are lifelines; the questbook borrows only a glance. §r%n%n§8§oThe end of beekeeping is a beauty pageant, judged by the questbook.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAARg.name=§1§lThe Sun Never Sets
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAARg.desc=512 panes of glass — a crystal palace's declaration: from now on the sun never sets over your roof.%n%nShow §1 512§r glass — page one of the megaproject manifesto. Reward: §1 16 sets§r of lithography material, the palace's wiring.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. But warehousing 512 glass is the manifesto's first hurdle. §r%n%n§8§oEvery empire on which the sun never sets begins with one pane.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAARw.name=§c§lDeclaration of the Blade
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAARw.desc=Some materials are born to be the edge, others to be the point. Eight plus eight: the blade's declaration is written in two metals, signed with your name.%n%nShow §1 8§r blade alloy and §1 8§r edge stock — display-only. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The blade says nothing; the storage drawer remembers. §r%n%n§8§oA declaration's sharpness depends on the metal's patience.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAASA.name=§1§lThe Coal Manifesto
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAASA.desc=1024 coal — an epoch's worth of burning, stacked into a black mountain. The last love letter to the steam age.%n%nShow §1 1024§r coal — display-only. Reward: §1 16§r coal blocks, the letter pressed into amber.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Coal freedom is not energy freedom — do not get carried away burning. §r%n%n§8§oCoal's end is not ash but an agenda.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAASQ.name=§c§lThe Cobalt Edge
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAASQ.desc=Cobalt's blue is the prelude to a cold edge. The blade manifesto's second chapter is written on two lines: ore and alloy.%n%nShow §1 4§r cobalt plates and §1 64§r iron ore — display-only. Reward: §1 16 sets§r of LV circuits, a pleasantly retro return gift.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Cobalt's supply chain is harder to please than its color. §r%n%n§8§oBlue is never gentle — least of all on metal.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAASg.name=§d§lPearls Without End!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAASg.desc=64 pearl workings plus 16 sheets of paper, bound into Pearls Without End — the Endermen's genealogy, fourth edition, yours.%n%nShow §1 64§r pearl parts and §1 16§r paper — display-only. Reward: §1 32§r ender pearls and §1 4§r name tags.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The end of pearls is the void; the end of the void is storage anxiety. §r%n%n§8§oPearls are cheap — the expensive part is the word "without end".§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAASw.name=§2§lThe Emerald Pact
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAASw.desc=64 emeralds and a paper pact with the villagers: even in the age of machines, green still matters.%n%nShow §1 64§r emeralds — display-only. Reward: §1 2 shimmering coins§r, green finance's interest.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Do not pass emeralds off as diamonds — the questbook is colorblind, not blind. §r%n%n§8§oThe Emerald Pact: interest settled in shimmering coins, fair to all ages.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAATA.name=§1§lThe Iron Epic
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAATA.desc=1024 iron ingots — counted from the first, your entire opening history. The Iron Epic's final chapter is a warehousing problem.%n%nShow §1 1024§r iron ingots — display-only. Reward: §1 16§r iron blocks, the epic's hardcover edition.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The epic charges no admission but eats backpack space.%n%n§8§oThe epic's last page always reads "to be continued".§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAATQ.name=§3§lFree Wireless EU
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAATQ.desc=§3GTSWN§r's stage: a wall of cables traded for a field of wireless freedom. Nothing to submit here — just sign in.%n%nClick to complete and join. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r; the membership fee runs backwards.%n%n§cWarning: wireless is not maintenance-free — dead zones and red-line power levels persist. §r%n%n§8§oMore supplies at the vending machine's matching pages. Cable retirement ceremonies self-funded.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAATg.name=§3§lPocket-Sized Oversight
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAATg.desc=The grid's health report now fits in your pocket. Pocket oversight: wherever you walk, whatever the watt.%n%nShow §1 1§r portable wireless network monitor — display-only. Reward: §1 2§r sensors, oversight's expansion pack.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The overseer reports but never repairs; breakdowns are still yours in person. §r%n%n§8§oPocket oversight: an ECG of the whole grid in your pouch.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAATw.name=§3§lWatchdog Watts
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAATw.desc=Comparators are redstone's eyes and the grid's watchdogs. Four on duty together, day and night shifts — when watts sleep, they don't.%n%nHand in §1 4§r comparators for §1 8§r glowstone dust — the watchdogs' night-shift bonus.%n%n§cWarning: the comparators are consumed. Recruit replacements before the redstone shift ends. §r%n%n§8§oWatchdogs bite no one — only anomalous signals.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUA.name=§3§lTrends on a Wall
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUA.desc=Data asleep in ledgers wakes up on walls. The info panel: your grid's trend chart.%n%nCraft §1 1§r network info panel — §3GTSWN§r's roadside show. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: the panel displays but decides nothing. The trend chart is lovely; so is the power bill. §r%n%n§8§oHanging candlestick charts in Minecraft: the engineer's romance.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUQ.name=§3§lThe Bigger Picture
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUQ.desc=One panel not enough? Extenders widen the picture until the whole workshop lives on the wall.%n%nCraft §1 2§r info panel extenders. Reward: §1 8§r of the same back — the full wall's budget covered at once.%n%n§cWarning: extenders extend the picture, not the throughput. Bigger screen, clearer responsibility. §r%n%n§8§oThe big-screen era's chronic ailment: watching the chart, forgetting the generator.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUg.name=§d§lThe Quantum Estate
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUg.desc=Wire an ME network terminal into the wireless grid — the quantum estate's foundation, and the estate has no walls.%n%nCraft §1 1§r ME Network Quantum Terminal — §3GTSWN§r shaking hands with §dthe quantum§r.%n%n§cWarning: quantum terminals are delicate; verify the voltage tier before wiring in. §r%n%n§8§oThe estate's end is quantum; quantum's end is the estate.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUw.name=§3§lThe Machine Ledger
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUw.desc=Every machine's model, status and breakdown history, all filed in one ledger. The device terminal: the workshop's HR archive.%n%nShow §1 1§r device info terminal — display-only. Reward: §1 1§r of the same, bookkeepers in pairs.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The ledger records machines; the one leafing through it is still you. §r%n%n§8§oLedger-keeping: the cyberpunk edition of pastoral poetry.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAVA.name=§6§lMake Steam Great Again!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAVA.desc=§6GTSR§r's stage: steam never expired — it just changed posts. Make steam great again, starting with this check-in.%n%nClick to complete and join. Reward: §1 2§r Steam Entangled Singularities and §1 2 neko coins§r — founding dividends.%n%n§cWarning: GTSR gates no era; come and go freely. The steam party collects no dues, only dividends. §r%n%n§8§oMore supplies at the vending machine's matching pages. Long live the boiler.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAVQ.name=§6§lOvertime for the Sun
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAVQ.desc=Sunset is not a reason — it is an excuse. The large solar array: putting the sun on night shifts.%n%nShow §1 1§r large solar unit — display-only. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r, overtime billed to the sun's account.%n%n§cWarning: solar night shifts run on daytime surplus — do not skimp on the storage tanks. §r%n%n§8§oSun: I never agreed to overtime. GTSR: agreeing to shine is enough.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAVg.name=§6§lZenith of the Sun
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAVg.desc=One unit is a pilot; eight are a legion. When the mirror farm covers the roof, the sun reaches its zenith.%n%nShow §1 8§r large solar units — display-only. Reward: §1 4 neko coins§r, the legion's payroll.%n%n§cWarning: eight units paralleled draw a nasty inrush — do the fuse math first. §r%n%n§8§oPast the zenith is high noon; past high noon, eternal daylight.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAVw.name=§6§lMagma into Steam
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAVw.desc=Wasting magma's heat is a shame; the geothermal overheat chip teaches it to work: magma in, steam out, loop closed.%n%nShow §1 1§r magma-steam unit and §1 1§r Geothermal Overheat Chip. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: the overheat chip lives up to its name — fail the thermal management and it strikes first. §r%n%n§8§oThe planet's fury, piped straight into your boiler.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWA.name=§6§lThe Four-to-One Gate
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWA.desc=Four steam sources, one master gate. The gate controller turns skirmishers into a regular army — four branch lines now answer one whistle.%n%nShow §1 1§r gate controller — display-only. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: the master gate's dispatch logic sets the downstream's floor. §r%n%n§8§oFour-to-one is not a compression ratio — it is discipline.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWQ.name=§6§lOne-Ticket Direct
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWQ.desc=The hub terminal: one ticket, every platform of the steam economy. The official sequel to White-Glove Delivery.%n%nShow §1 1§r Hub Terminal — display-only. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Once the terminal is in, the "Singularity Exchange" page gains a hub-chip resupply tier. §r%n%n§8§oThe price of one-ticket direct: a drawer forever stuffed with stubs.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWg.name=§6§lCross-Dimensional Drilling
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWg.desc=Ore underfoot, and more ore elsewhere. Cross-dimensional drilling: treating other dimensions' veins as your backyard.%n%nShow §1 1§r drilling hub — display-only. Reward: §1 4 neko coins§r, the interdimensional freight.%n%n§cWarning: cross-dimensional bills are booked per dimension — keep them separate. §r%n%n§8§oTo a drill bit, the distance between dimensions is a suggestion.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWw.name=§6§lCreation from Thin Air
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWw.desc=The crust material unit: turning the dirt and stone beneath you into industrial feedstock. Creation from thin air is really just sourcing on-site.%n%nShow §1 1§r material unit — display-only. Reward: §1 4 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: creation from thin air drinks power like water; bank a generation surplus first. §r%n%n§8§oTurning stone to gold is myth; turning mud to material is engineering.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXA.name=§6§lThe Ever-Faster Furnace
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXA.desc=A common coke oven burns a batch in one incense stick; the large one needs half. "Ever faster" is its motto.%n%nShow §1 1§r large coke oven — display-only. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: a faster oven eats coke faster too — keep the supply chain up. §r%n%n§8§oA coke oven's speed is speed bought with coal.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXQ.name=§6§lCluster Mobilization
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXQ.desc=One building holding an entire production line — the cluster controller is that building's property manager and mayor.%n%nShow §1 1§r cluster controller — display-only. Reward: §1 8 neko coins§r, the mayoral stipend.%n%n§cWarning: the controller's management radius is finite; machines beyond it pretend not to know you. §r%n%n§8§oProperty fees collected in neko coins; service rendered to the whole tech tree.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXg.name=§6§lKinetic Processing Array
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXg.desc=One array, ten thousand recipes. The processing array is the workshop's Swiss army knife and the executioner of redundant bays — the machine roster is one line long now.%n%nShow §1 1§r processing array — display-only. Reward: §1 4 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: the array switches to a rhythm; hard stops and starts hurt the molds. §r%n%n§8§oThe price of versatility: the repairman must be versatile too.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXw.name=§c§lIgniting the Singularity Chain
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXw.desc=The steam entangler: a delivery room that twists surplus pressure into singularities. The chain's first link is lit.%n%nShow §1 1§r singularity entangler — display-only. Reward: §1 4 neko coins§r and §1 4§r singularities, the ignition gift.%n%n§cWarning: the entangler's startup surge is no joke — warm up the grid first. §r%n%n§8§oWith the chain lit, the "Singularity Exchange" page gains the 16-singularity bulk tier.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYA.name=§c§lA Thousand to One
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYA.desc=A thousand shares of steam pressure for one miracle. The deep-pressure unit's exchange rate out-cuts any bank.%n%nShow §1 1§r deep-pressure unit — display-only. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r.%n%n§cWarning: thousand-to-one exchanges do not reverse — count your zeros before ordering. §r%n%n§8§oFinancial freedom means surviving a 1000:1 exchange rate.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYQ.name=§c§lCritical Mass
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYQ.desc=The critical steam unit: the closer of chain reactions. At this step your steam empire keeps nuclear-grade books.%n%nShow §1 1§r critical steam unit — display-only. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r.%n%n§cWarning: criticals are counted by the dozen — and the "critical singularity for 32 shimmering" tier unlocks along the way. §r%n%n§8§oThe end of mass is energy; the end of energy is neko coins.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYg.name=§6§lNeko Coins!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYg.desc=§6§lGT-Interesting-Thing§r: one vending machine, two coins, and ten ring slots for ten fingers.%n%nNeko coins come from loot chests, fishing and daily sign-ins; the §dshimmering coin§r is their golden upper crust. This one is on the house — take it, save up §1sixty-four§r, then come back and talk exchange rates.%n%n§cWarning: wallet balance never fills your backpack, but it is team-shared — you and your mates are spending the same purse. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the machine's "Periodic Supplies" page. Every true cat lives payday to payday.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYw.name=§2§lUnboxing Surprise
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYw.desc=A welcome gift unboxed a second time is still a surprise — the cat's hamper never ships empty.%n%nShow §1 1§r starter gift — display-only. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r, the recycling corner's friendly price.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Hamper contents are random; mysticism carries no warranty. §r%n%n§8§oThe joy of unboxing, second time, no discount.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAZA.name=§6§lDaily Check-In
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAZA.desc=The neko vending machine: GTNH's 24-hour convenience store. Day one of check-ins begins with bringing it home.%n%nShow §1 1§r vending machine — display-only. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r, the opening flower basket.%n%n§cWarning: the machine wants power and ME — settle the interfaces before talking business hours. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the "Periodic Supplies" premium tier — restocked every 22 hours.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAZQ.name=§d§lWiring the Cat into ME
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAZQ.desc=The machine honors coins and networks alike. Wire in the ME uplink bay and the cat's stock pipes straight into your quantum estate.%n%nShow §1 1§r ME uplink bay — display-only. Reward: §1 4 neko coins§r, the interface fee.%n%n§cWarning: the uplink bay is the machine's throat — offline means out of stock. §r%n%n§8§oStep one of the Internet of Things: connect the cat first.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAZg.name=§2§lSixty-Four in the Wallet
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAZg.desc=64 neko coins — the wallet's first slot at full capacity. Gather them, then head back to the GTIT hub to talk exchange rates.%n%nShow §1 64§r neko coins — display-only. Reward: §1 1 shimmering coin§r plus §1 56§r in change; the rate is settled.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. The machine's built-in rate table cheats neither old nor young. §r%n%n§8§oCoin-savings freedom is station one of financial freedom.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAZw.name=§d§lLord of the Rings!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAZw.desc=Ten fingers, ten ring slots. GTIT's ring system: start with one, crown yourself with the set.%n%nShow §1 1§r Skywalk Ring — display-only. Reward: §1 2 neko coins§r and §1 1§r ring of your choice.%n%n§cWarning: ring slots are finite — plan today's loadout before heading out. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the machine's basic "Ring Repurchase" tier.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAaA.name=§d§lThe Art of Stacking
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAaA.desc=Ring effects stack across fingers: Distant Grasp in pairs, Ironheart in pairs. The art of stacking prizes symmetry.%n%nShow §1 2§r Distant Grasp rings and §1 2§r Ironheart rings — display-only. Reward: §1 4 neko coins§r.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Stacked effects depend on luck — and on free slots. §r%n%n§8§oSymmetry is aesthetics, and the first principle of combat theory.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAaQ.name=§d§lAura Trifecta
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAaQ.desc=Dragon's Breath, Tempest, Mountainbreaker — three aura rings in one frame, the ring world's family portrait.%n%nShow §1 1§r of each aura ring — display-only. Reward: §1 4 neko coins§r, studio portrait rates.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Aura effects are invisible; the invoice is not. §r%n%n§8§oChoose your own pose for the triple shot — the questbook counts heads.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAag.name=§d§lWindrider, the Final Ring
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAag.desc=The terminus of seven rings: the final ring, Windrider. The moment it is crafted, the ring slots close their loop.%n%nCraft §1 1§r Windrider Ring. Reward: §1 2 shimmering coins§r and §1 8 neko coins§r — the coronation's gift money.%n%n§cWarning: the materials are dear and the questbook reimburses nothing — though the machine stocks a materials tier. §r%n%n§8§oCompleting this quest unlocks the materials pack: one purchase only (maxTrades=1).§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAaw.name=§d§lThe Infinite Cell!
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAaw.desc=The end of items is storage; the end of storage is the infinity cell. One cell, one category, §1Integer.MAX_VALUE§r items.%n%nShow §1 1§r infinity cell — display-only. Reward: §1 2 shimmering coins§r, the certificate of storage freedom.%n%n§cWarning: idle draw is §11 AE/t§r — check the meter before filling the bays. §r%n%n§8§oAfter this quest, the infinity cell pair enters the "Endgame Exchange" page at 48 shimmering coins each.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAbA.name=§3§lFollow the Map
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAbA.desc=The Mind's Eye swept the veins; now the maps close the file. Two maps, one treasure hunt's receipt.%n%nHand in §1 2§r maps for §1 4§r compasses — next time you are lost, at least the heading will be right.%n%n§cWarning: the maps are consumed. The cartographer's toil is duly appreciated. §r%n%n§8§oA map's end is not the treasure but the next coordinate.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAbQ.name=§2§lThe Weight of Shimmer
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAbQ.desc=Eight shimmering coins pressed into your palm teach you what weight means — the density of upper-tier currency.%n%nShow §1 8§r shimmering coins — display-only. Reward: §1 4 shimmering coins§r, interest on the weight.%n%n§cWarning: display-only. Shimmer flatters no one by mistake — only those who can save it. §r%n%n§8§oWhat shimmers is not the coin but the days of saving.§r
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAbg.name=§6§lThe Master
betterquesting.quest.TUlBTwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAbg.desc=You burned through steam, lit up LV, left MV, HV, EV, IV in the dust, and finally §dLuV§r became old news. Behind you, three mod hubs have woven themselves into a single net.%n%nNow close this questbook. §6§lThe Master§r is not a quest — it is a commemorative coin, and the key to the vending machine's §d"Endgame Exchange"§r page: critical singularities, reinforced chips, infinity cells, nether stars, and that dragon egg.%n%n§cWarning: the endgame shelf is daily-limited — even masters obey the cooldown. §r%n%n§8§oHAJIMI HAJIMI. Enjoy the journey.§r
